---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Community | Artists, Collectors, Players & Researchers"
  description="Join the NO BALL GAMES community across street culture, Grime Art, digital collectibles, XRP KIDs lore, gaming and creative collaboration."
  current="community"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Community</span>
    <h1>For the people who played anyway.</h1>
    <p>
      The brand only works if people can take part. This page gives the community a clear place to understand the movement, follow updates and connect with future drops, lore threads and research work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section card-grid">
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Collectors</span>
      <h3>Own the archive</h3>
      <p>Collectors can follow physical and digital releases, limited drops, signed work and future reward mechanics. Every piece connects to the lore.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>Browse collections →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Artists</span>
      <h3>Build the wall</h3>
      <p>Artists, writers and designers can connect through collaborations, callouts, future challenges and shared street-culture energy. The wall is open.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Get involved →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs</span>
      <h3>Track the chain-side story</h3>
      <p>Collectors and lore readers can follow the XRP KIDs branch, the 100 / 89 / 11 canon and the Alpha Aaron / FRET conflict without confusing fiction for verified ledger data.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Read the XRP page →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">Researchers</span>
      <h3>Help keep the truth file sharp</h3>
      <p>Archive builders, source hunters and long-memory community members can help separate verified facts, internal canon and source-needed claims.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}research/`}>Open the research vault →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Community engine</span>
      <h2>Give people something to do.</h2>
      <p>
        A good community page does not just say "follow us." It creates actions: collect, submit, vote, play, share, decode, join, win, collaborate and come back.
      </p>
      <p>
        NO BALL GAMES is building toward a community layer with real mechanics — not just a link to a platform.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Future actions</span>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Join the mailing list for early drop access.</li>
        <li>Submit wall photos, sign photos or street-culture references.</li>
        <li>Take part in community art challenges.</li>
        <li>Help verify XRP KIDs and archive claims before they are presented as fact.</li>
        <li>Follow drops, giveaways, lore reveals and collector announcements.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Stay connected</span>
      <h2>Don't miss the next drop.</h2>
      <p>Community updates, drop announcements, lore reveals, truth-file updates and collector opportunities — reach out to get on the list before things go public.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Get in touch</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}research/`}>Read the archive</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
